<%# The masthead both edition pages wear: the nameplate and the two ways off
    the page on one ruled band, the line naming this page on a second.

    The nav does not change shape between the edition and the archive, so the
    reader learns one navigation and the archive is always one click away —
    the same reason the feed's filters both stay on screen. The nameplate is
    the way back to the day's briefing, as a newspaper's is, which is what
    keeps an edition opened out of the archive from being a page with no way
    forward. %>
<header class="edition-masthead">
  <div class="edition-masthead__bar">
    <%= link_to root_path, class: "edition-masthead__home" do %>
      <%= render "application/lockup", size: 24 %>
    <% end %>

    <nav class="edition-masthead__nav">
      <%= link_to t("editions.header.archive"), editions_path,
            class: "edition-masthead__link" %>
      <%= link_to t("editions.header.originals"), newsletters_path,
            class: "edition-masthead__link" %>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <%# Set in mono, so uppercased by CSS rather than shouted in the locale
      file. %>
  <h1 class="edition-masthead__line"><%= line %></h1>
</header>
